WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY

No dataset is redistributed. data/raw/ holds one manifest per dataset -- its
source, its licence, the checksums of the files, and what was measured from
them -- and py/ holds the scripts that fetch them. The terms differ per
dataset and two of them matter:

  ZINC22 (files.docking.org) permits screening and the sharing of screening
  results, and requires written permission from John Irwin to redistribute
  large portions. The tranche this project reads is named in
  data/raw/zinc22/manifest.json so it can be fetched rather than copied.

  ChEMBL source 40 is CC BY-SA 3.0, whose share-alike would reach anything
  distributed with it. Nothing here reads it, and it is declared out of the
  evidence inventory for that reason as well.

The rest -- CHAMP, GramNegAccum, B3DB, IMI-COMBINE -- are CC BY 4.0, CC0 and
MIT, and are cited in their manifests. Attribution for each is in the
manifest's own attribution_required field.
